# ZSA keyboards -- the Moonlander, the Voyager -- and the Moonlander's
# bootloader, opened to whoever is sitting at the machine.
#
# Installed by the jayos-moonlander package into /usr/lib/udev/rules.d. JayOS
# builds the package only from its Moonlander setup in the control room, by
# the owner's call on 2026-10-26 that nothing of the Moonlander's is installed
# until somebody opts in there, so the rule arrives when the setup is run and
# not before. Until 2026-11-12 JayOS's root helper wrote it into
# /etc/udev/rules.d (jayos-app-install's zsa-rule verb, now gone); a copy left
# there masks this one by basename and says the same. Keymapp has to open the
# keyboard to read its layer, light it or flash it, and kontroll, the layer
# popups and JayOS's held-Super panel all ask Keymapp. `jayos-moonlander
# access` says which rule opens it.
#
# WHY THIS AND NOT ZSA's OWN. Keymapp's AUR package, zsa-keymapp-bin, depends on
# zsa-udev, whose rules give the keyboard to the group plugdev. Arch does not
# create that group, so on a stock machine they open the keyboard to nobody,
# and Keymapp starts and cannot see it -- which reads as a keyboard that is not
# plugged in. Read from the AUR's files on 2026-10-21.
#
# uaccess, as JayOS's 70-dualsense-hidraw.rules does and for its reasons:
# logind gives the seated user an ACL on the node and takes it back at logout,
# with no group to create or join and nothing for an ssh session. The tag is
# acted on by systemd's 73-seat-late.rules, which is why this file sorts
# before 73.
#
# NOT named 50-oryx.rules or 50-wally.rules, zsa-udev's names: two packages
# cannot own one path, and in /etc a shared name would mask that package's
# rules rather than sit beside them.
#
# 3297 is ZSA's vendor id: the keyboard's raw HID node, which ATTRS finds on
# the USB device above it, and the USB device itself, which is also how the
# Voyager's bootloader appears. 0483:df11 is the STM32 DFU bootloader the
# Moonlander restarts into to be flashed.
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="3297", TAG+="uaccess"
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="3297", TAG+="uaccess"
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="0483", ATTR{idProduct}=="df11", TAG+="uaccess"
